<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's coffee exports down 28.3 pct in Jan-Feb.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's coffee exports down 28.3 pct in Jan-Feb.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's coffee exports fell 28.3 percent in the first two months of 1997 to 116,389 60-kg bags due to the retention plan of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC), an exporters group said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The National Coffee Exporter Association said Ecuador shipped 162,347 bags in the first two months of 1996.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, coffee revenues fell 43.7 percent in the January-February period to $9.47 million from $16.83 million in the comparable period of 1996.</p>
<p>In 1996, Ecuador's coffee exports fell to 1.56 million 60-kg bags from 1.9 million bags exported in 1995.</p>
<p>Ecuador plans to export 1.4 million bags between July 1996 and June 1997.</p>
<p>Coffee is Ecuador's fifth export earner, after oil, banana, shrimp and cacao.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
